1
00:00:22,815 --> 00:00:23,135
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

2
00:00:23,175 --> 00:00:33,884
[SPEAKER_01]: So, I have one subject that was to do with, you know, these five reflections that are given for layperson and monk alike.

3
00:00:33,964 --> 00:00:44,813
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the first four to do with recollecting that I am subject to aging, knock on beyond aging, subject to illness, knock on beyond illness, subject to

4
00:00:45,938 --> 00:00:50,261
[SPEAKER_01]: Death and thus I will be separated from all that's dear to me.

5
00:00:50,421 --> 00:01:05,970
[SPEAKER_01]: But now my question is particularly in regard to the last one, which says I am the owner of my actions, heir to my actions, born of my actions, kin to my actions, and my actions are my shelter.

6
00:01:08,611 --> 00:01:08,792
[SPEAKER_01]: And

7
00:01:12,049 --> 00:01:19,345
[SPEAKER_01]: So, I recently heard that explained in a way that surprised me a little bit, because it was sort of as a...

8
00:01:21,071 --> 00:01:37,714
[SPEAKER_01]: Particularly Buddhist reflection on, you know, something that would have to be taken on faith, that, you know, you're... if you do good, good things will happen to you in the future, and it's kind of an encouragement.

9
00:01:38,735 --> 00:01:41,055
[SPEAKER_01]: And I hadn't seen it in that way.

10
00:01:42,975 --> 00:01:49,677
[SPEAKER_01]: So, I was wondering if you could talk about the extent to which this type of reflection

11
00:01:50,882 --> 00:01:56,027
[SPEAKER_01]: And, maybe, karma, more generally, is something that is directly visible.

12
00:01:59,124 --> 00:02:06,550
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, yeah, it's definitely much... goes deeper than just, you know, do good and good will come to you.

13
00:02:06,990 --> 00:02:17,638
[SPEAKER_00]: Especially, like, if... especially paired with all the other reflections that are quite direct and acute, you know, everything that is there will become otherwise and so on.

14
00:02:18,338 --> 00:02:22,601
[SPEAKER_00]: That's not... that's not a type of reflection that the Buddha would just give to a casual lay person.

15
00:02:23,362 --> 00:02:23,582
[SPEAKER_00]: And...

16
00:02:24,949 --> 00:02:28,610
[SPEAKER_00]: He would give to a casual lay person, ah, do good and you'll be reborn in heaven.

17
00:02:29,210 --> 00:02:38,593
[SPEAKER_00]: So, since this whole thing about karma is paired with such direct instructions of reflection with how to approve the ownership and so on, means it's on the same level.

18
00:02:39,193 --> 00:02:44,495
[SPEAKER_00]: So, and as the suttas say, basically, every action is intention.

19
00:02:45,215 --> 00:02:48,816
[SPEAKER_00]: So, anything that comes out of your intention is your karma.

20
00:02:50,257 --> 00:02:52,758
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's why you need to really

21
00:02:54,953 --> 00:03:00,518
[SPEAKER_00]: Understand and take on the weight of it, just on the level of intentions.

22
00:03:01,038 --> 00:03:05,602
[SPEAKER_00]: Because, see, people think I'm not doing any bad karma, because, you know, I'm not killing, I'm not stealing.

23
00:03:05,662 --> 00:03:09,625
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, that's true by body, but how about speech, how about the mind?

24
00:03:10,266 --> 00:03:19,374
[SPEAKER_00]: And given that now we're talking about the reflections that are directly relevant to the practice, you know, like I'm subject to aging, death, sickness, everything that's there will change.

25
00:03:19,514 --> 00:03:22,697
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay, time is short, I'm running out of time, I better do something about it.

26
00:03:23,397 --> 00:03:30,101
[SPEAKER_00]: In the same sense, karma relates on that same level, if it's taken on the level of your intention, the weight of it.

27
00:03:30,361 --> 00:03:40,708
[SPEAKER_00]: So, I am the owner of my actions, means, okay, so each time I intend, even by thought, to do something unwholesome, I will be the owner of that.

28
00:03:41,828 --> 00:03:52,435
[SPEAKER_00]: That will be the sole reason that I'm still not uprooting the, you know, suffering on account of losing what is dear to me, or suffering on account of losing health or life and so on.

29
00:03:53,455 --> 00:03:58,857
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's the... yeah, it's a very... it's a very direct, very acute and very unpleasant reflection.

30
00:04:00,317 --> 00:04:04,239
[SPEAKER_00]: Because... and also, probably the subtlest.

31
00:04:04,559 --> 00:04:13,542
[SPEAKER_00]: You can, you know, even... even somebody who doesn't want to see, with some effort, you can see the subject being subject to aging, to sickness, to death.

32
00:04:14,282 --> 00:04:17,143
[SPEAKER_00]: You need to sort of, you know, dwell on it until it sinks in.

33
00:04:18,056 --> 00:04:26,805
[SPEAKER_00]: But, taking on the weight of kāma on the level of your intentions, and these mental choices, that people don't really feel... like, it doesn't feel like a big deal.

34
00:04:26,865 --> 00:04:31,570
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, you need to start regarding it as a big deal, if you want to be truly free, and completely free.

35
00:04:31,830 --> 00:04:35,674
[SPEAKER_01]: Even that very first one, I am the owner of my actions.

36
00:04:35,974 --> 00:04:40,559
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, I, nobody else, owner of what I do, in the sense, like,

37
00:04:42,278 --> 00:04:43,159
[SPEAKER_01]: I can't really...

38
00:04:43,219 --> 00:04:44,962
[SPEAKER_01]: I cannot put it on anybody else.

39
00:04:45,042 --> 00:04:53,213
[SPEAKER_01]: There is nothing... nothing else that I can sort of blame or kind of...

40
00:04:54,093 --> 00:05:04,161
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, nobody can come in between, nobody can take part of it on... always it's all... it's because of this, or because of that, or... oh, well, you know, yes, some of it is my fault, but some of it is their fault.

41
00:05:04,421 --> 00:05:12,387
[SPEAKER_00]: As far as your intentions are concerned, and the results of your actions, so, as far as saṃsāra is concerned, it's all on you.

42
00:05:12,727 --> 00:05:13,968
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever you do, it's only on you.

43
00:05:15,242 --> 00:05:15,742
[SPEAKER_01]: So, no matter how much...

44
00:05:15,762 --> 00:05:16,423
[SPEAKER_00]: There's no excuse.

45
00:05:17,564 --> 00:05:28,811
[SPEAKER_00]: Sort of, oh, it was a very difficult external circumstance... Yeah, well, like the Buddha said, even if the highway robbers are chopping your limbs, if you have the thoughts of hate, you are not... you are the one who hasn't freed yourself.

46
00:05:29,572 --> 00:05:30,693
[SPEAKER_00]: It doesn't matter what they do.

47
00:05:31,313 --> 00:05:34,095
[SPEAKER_00]: It doesn't matter what choices... well, it matters for them, not for you.

48
00:05:35,862 --> 00:05:39,403
[SPEAKER_00]: So, yeah, it needs to be taken in that absolute sense.

49
00:05:41,024 --> 00:05:46,686
[SPEAKER_01]: And that part too, like, I am the heir of my actions paired with the others.

50
00:05:48,206 --> 00:06:02,371
[SPEAKER_01]: I was thinking it's actually quite heavy, quite important, as in this situation that I'm currently in, that is a danger subject to all of these things.

51
00:06:02,712 --> 00:06:03,712
[SPEAKER_00]: All these liabilities.

52
00:06:04,453 --> 00:06:09,417
[SPEAKER_01]: That's actually something that is already on me somehow.

53
00:06:09,718 --> 00:06:10,659
[SPEAKER_00]: Because of the actions.

54
00:06:10,879 --> 00:06:11,179
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

55
00:06:11,539 --> 00:06:13,461
[SPEAKER_00]: Because of these actions that I'm not free from.

56
00:06:14,122 --> 00:06:17,124
[SPEAKER_00]: And I'm not free from them because I've been avoiding responsibility for them.

57
00:06:17,825 --> 00:06:22,549
[SPEAKER_00]: So, in order to free myself first, I need to take on the full weight of... No, no, no.

58
00:06:23,250 --> 00:06:23,750
[SPEAKER_00]: It's on me.

59
00:06:24,811 --> 00:06:31,640
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm the owner of my actions, I'm the heir to them, whatever I do, the action, the results of those actions, so there is nothing to it.

60
00:06:32,260 --> 00:06:34,884
[SPEAKER_00]: I really need to take the full responsibility.

61
00:06:35,785 --> 00:06:43,274
[SPEAKER_00]: And that takes even more sinking in than the previous reflections, because it doesn't feel like it's your fault.

62
00:06:44,195 --> 00:06:46,116
[SPEAKER_00]: It doesn't feel like it's your responsibility.

63
00:06:46,756 --> 00:06:47,977
[SPEAKER_00]: It doesn't feel the weight.

64
00:06:48,357 --> 00:06:54,502
[SPEAKER_00]: It doesn't feel heavy, like when you have these little thoughts of desire and intentions and delights and so on.

65
00:06:54,982 --> 00:06:56,503
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just these fleeting little things.

66
00:06:56,583 --> 00:06:58,865
[SPEAKER_00]: Most of the time, I don't have that, but it doesn't matter.

67
00:06:59,525 --> 00:07:05,910
[SPEAKER_00]: You need to take it in a serious sense, whereby, as the Buddha said, yeah, if you, you know, if you if you if you're sort of covered in mud and dirt,

68
00:07:07,890 --> 00:07:12,996
[SPEAKER_00]: You know, removing a little bit doesn't doesn't mean much, because you're all still absolutely covered in filth.

69
00:07:13,576 --> 00:07:22,806
[SPEAKER_00]: But now imagine you're completely clean, you have a pure white cloth, one tiny little stain will stand out, will be a big deal, will be visible from every angle.

70
00:07:23,367 --> 00:07:24,528
[SPEAKER_00]: Because everything else is clean.

71
00:07:24,628 --> 00:07:25,309
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's the point.

72
00:07:25,369 --> 00:07:31,494
[SPEAKER_00]: If you have been practicing to the point of, you know, subject to aging, sickness, death, everything is dear to me.

73
00:07:31,614 --> 00:07:46,608
[SPEAKER_00]: If you've been enduring it, valuing it, contemplating it, understanding it, then, yeah, you will realize the weight even of these little fleeting thoughts and intentions that you do welcome, that you do accept, that you do sort of choose to engage with, at least mentally.

74
00:07:47,248 --> 00:07:58,294
[SPEAKER_00]: Sometimes verbally, sometimes maybe physically, but point is, okay, so I am not uprooting the main reason that I am liable to all these things that I've been contemplating beforehand.

75
00:08:00,015 --> 00:08:05,479
[SPEAKER_01]: By engaging in this, oh, I am maintaining these, this suffering that I am still subject to.

76
00:08:05,499 --> 00:08:06,299
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly, yeah, yeah.

77
00:08:06,639 --> 00:08:12,903
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, yeah, more, let's say, more generally, karma, karma is often

78
00:08:15,889 --> 00:08:16,990
[SPEAKER_01]: That's because people confuse.

79
00:08:32,892 --> 00:08:40,478
[SPEAKER_00]: The understanding with workings of karma, they confuse that with understanding the nature of action.

80
00:08:41,178 --> 00:08:42,359
[SPEAKER_00]: And those are two separate things.

81
00:08:42,940 --> 00:08:48,904
[SPEAKER_00]: But people think that, aha, if I understand how karma works, I thus understood what karma is.

82
00:08:49,745 --> 00:08:50,626
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's not the case.

83
00:08:51,426 --> 00:08:56,209
[SPEAKER_00]: So, when the Buddha said, if you try to understand the workings of kamma, you would meet only madness or distraction.

84
00:08:56,409 --> 00:08:56,850
[SPEAKER_00]: There is not...

85
00:08:57,210 --> 00:09:00,272
[SPEAKER_00]: But then, on many other occasions, he said, he understood kamma.

86
00:09:00,832 --> 00:09:05,295
[SPEAKER_00]: He understood the nature of action, the root of it, and approached it.

87
00:09:05,775 --> 00:09:06,936
[SPEAKER_00]: So, those are two different things.

88
00:09:07,577 --> 00:09:17,843
[SPEAKER_00]: If people are not aware of that, they will then, sort of, approach understanding of the nature of kamma, through just collecting information about the workings of kamma, and repercussions of kamma, and so on.

89
00:09:17,883 --> 00:09:19,024
[SPEAKER_00]: And that has nothing to do with it.

90
00:09:20,290 --> 00:09:20,450
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

91
00:09:20,870 --> 00:09:25,753
[SPEAKER_01]: And if you understand the nature of karma, then you realize that the workings of it are totally irrelevant.

92
00:09:25,773 --> 00:09:26,133
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

93
00:09:26,353 --> 00:09:28,755
[SPEAKER_00]: It doesn't matter which way it works, because you're free from it.

94
00:09:29,155 --> 00:09:32,217
[SPEAKER_00]: The only reason you were concerned with the workings is because you knew you were not free.

95
00:09:33,197 --> 00:09:36,879
[SPEAKER_00]: You were under its pressure, under its control, and it was unpleasant and it was painful.

96
00:09:37,920 --> 00:09:41,502
[SPEAKER_01]: I think a problem with the idea that it's something that is sort of a

97
00:09:43,483 --> 00:09:43,763
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

98
00:09:44,363 --> 00:09:57,650
[SPEAKER_01]: The thing that is just or maybe you take it on faith, maybe you get the results or not, and not seeing it on that direct level, is that it sort of prevents you from seeing this.

99
00:09:58,290 --> 00:09:59,711
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, yeah, like you just said this.

100
00:10:00,767 --> 00:10:02,108
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, you won't realize the depth of it.

101
00:10:02,208 --> 00:10:02,408
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

102
00:10:02,628 --> 00:10:04,890
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's just gonna stay on the surface and fine.

103
00:10:05,310 --> 00:10:15,618
[SPEAKER_00]: And, again, it's... see, the misunderstanding in that way results in kind of... you obviously, sooner or later, gonna think that, okay, yeah, you fulfill that requirement.

104
00:10:16,038 --> 00:10:17,679
[SPEAKER_00]: Because I do think about my karma.

105
00:10:17,699 --> 00:10:19,600
[SPEAKER_00]: I do good and, you know, good will come to me.

106
00:10:20,141 --> 00:10:21,161
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's what the Buddha meant.

107
00:10:21,201 --> 00:10:21,702
[SPEAKER_00]: Full stop.

108
00:10:24,291 --> 00:10:48,449
[SPEAKER_00]: But actually, you realize, if you were to then consider what if it meant even more, and start pushing it for further, and you come to realize it's the weight of your own intentional, like, responsibility behind your intentions and choices by mind, then you realize, ah, okay, yeah, so if I actually have put it on that level, then I've truly, sort of, freed myself from kamma, in that sense.

109
00:10:50,630 --> 00:10:54,013
[SPEAKER_01]: And you can even see how, you know, this, the...

110
00:10:56,508 --> 00:11:04,324
[SPEAKER_01]: The situation you're in now, the ways that things have, the suffering, the way that suffering hits you, is kind of...

111
00:11:05,148 --> 00:11:11,191
[SPEAKER_01]: Quite directly a result of the way that you have been acting, and the things that you have been cultivating.

112
00:11:11,211 --> 00:11:31,280
[SPEAKER_00]: Not necessarily the immediate result, but it's certainly, yeah, like, if you keep yourself, just a mundane example, if you keep yourself unfit and unhealthy, you will be more exposed, or rather, even the minimal exposure to elements will be much more painful, much harder to endure, much more overwhelming, much more bothersome.

113
00:11:32,402 --> 00:11:34,362
[SPEAKER_00]: Because the mind hasn't been developed.

114
00:11:34,502 --> 00:11:35,983
[SPEAKER_00]: In this sense, the body hasn't been developed.

115
00:11:36,003 --> 00:11:43,964
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the voice is the same when the mind hasn't been developed, when the mind has not practiced sensory strength in regard to desire, in regard to acting out of will, ill will.

116
00:11:44,304 --> 00:11:45,925
[SPEAKER_00]: Every little thing will then provoke you.

117
00:11:46,445 --> 00:11:51,346
[SPEAKER_00]: Every little thing will induce passion and pressure and pain, because, yeah, it proliferates.

118
00:11:51,546 --> 00:11:56,527
[SPEAKER_00]: The more you give into it, the wilder... the more you allow the wild animal to run free, the wilder it will become.

119
00:11:58,447 --> 00:12:01,448
[SPEAKER_01]: I can illustrate maybe the... an example thus...

120
00:12:03,174 --> 00:12:16,569
[SPEAKER_01]: Occurred for me recent... not that recently, but a few months ago, I was in seclusion at one point, and at one point, my mind was just full

121
00:12:17,625 --> 00:12:26,348
[SPEAKER_01]: There were thoughts of unwholesome things that I had done or unwholesome ways I behaved in the past that I regretted, which was unpleasant.

122
00:12:27,689 --> 00:12:35,932
[SPEAKER_01]: And previously, I would have thought that I would have had to try not to have these thoughts and try to stop them.

123
00:12:36,592 --> 00:12:39,133
[SPEAKER_01]: At that point, fortunately enough, I had

124
00:12:39,997 --> 00:12:44,220
[SPEAKER_01]: I gained a little bit more wisdom, so I was not sort of trying to stop them, just trying to endure them.

125
00:12:44,260 --> 00:12:48,823
[SPEAKER_01]: But at one point, it occurred to me a sutta that I had read ages ago.

126
00:12:50,224 --> 00:13:03,953
[SPEAKER_01]: It was one of these where the Buddha sees a monk just sitting in the forest or something and he's... and it says this monk was experiencing sharp, piercing feelings

127
00:13:04,937 --> 00:13:06,899
[SPEAKER_01]: On account of his past wrong actions.

128
00:13:06,919 --> 00:13:07,119
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

129
00:13:07,559 --> 00:13:07,859
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

130
00:13:08,080 --> 00:13:13,965
[SPEAKER_01]: And I remember at the time when I read that, I had sort of thought of it as, oh, some kind of magical... Yeah, some physical torture.

131
00:13:13,985 --> 00:13:14,545
[SPEAKER_01]: Physical torture.

132
00:13:14,565 --> 00:13:15,866
[SPEAKER_00]: Like some spirits or something.

133
00:13:16,066 --> 00:13:16,407
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

134
00:13:16,827 --> 00:13:18,088
[SPEAKER_01]: And then I was like, wait a second.

135
00:13:18,488 --> 00:13:18,688
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

136
00:13:18,949 --> 00:13:19,569
[SPEAKER_01]: Here I am.

137
00:13:19,589 --> 00:13:19,689
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

138
00:13:20,110 --> 00:13:23,492
[SPEAKER_01]: Feeling unpleasant feelings on account of my past actions.

139
00:13:23,572 --> 00:13:25,794
[SPEAKER_01]: And it said in the sutta, he's patiently enduring them.

140
00:13:25,854 --> 00:13:26,055
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

141
00:13:26,075 --> 00:13:28,877
[SPEAKER_01]: So, here, okay, I have to patiently endure them.

142
00:13:28,917 --> 00:13:32,360
[SPEAKER_01]: You can see it on that kind of direct... My mind

143
00:13:33,380 --> 00:13:45,266
[SPEAKER_00]: Is kind of the results, accumulation of these past things, and it was quite... Well, simply, you see, like a possibility of regret is another result of your action, of any action.

144
00:13:46,207 --> 00:13:51,630
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's why, you know, the Buddha often talks about blamelessness and doing the actions, they will not be blameworthy, because

145
00:13:52,980 --> 00:14:08,905
[SPEAKER_00]: If they're blameworthy, sooner or later, if, you know, if you don't perpetually distract yourself up until the moment you die, the mind will become aware, and the regret and the weight of it will have to come, and it will be unpleasant, and it could have been avoided if you didn't act in the first place.

146
00:14:09,025 --> 00:14:09,625
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

147
00:14:10,345 --> 00:14:19,287
[SPEAKER_00]: And, but again, it's like people regard this vipāka, the result of the action, as some sort of, again, mystical retribution that comes later in time.

148
00:14:19,407 --> 00:14:21,088
[SPEAKER_00]: Vipāka simply means result.

149
00:14:22,232 --> 00:14:26,193
[SPEAKER_00]: So, in the same sense, now, I say, can you get up and pass me that bottle?

150
00:14:26,653 --> 00:14:31,114
[SPEAKER_00]: Everything that happens as a result of that action, will be the result of that action, from my point of view.

151
00:14:31,814 --> 00:14:37,275
[SPEAKER_00]: Getting the bottle of water, you say, maybe you get upset because I asked you something, I didn't ask you nicely.

152
00:14:37,715 --> 00:14:40,496
[SPEAKER_00]: That will be the result, from my point of view, of my action.

153
00:14:40,616 --> 00:14:44,016
[SPEAKER_00]: That is my vipāka, because it resulted.

154
00:14:44,436 --> 00:14:47,397
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, all I can do, I can't control those results.

155
00:14:48,057 --> 00:14:58,401
[SPEAKER_00]: But I can control, or make sure, that my initial action was not rooted in greed, aversion, I didn't make you do it to humiliate you, or because I hate you, or something like that.

156
00:14:59,202 --> 00:15:01,522
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, it doesn't matter which way it results.

157
00:15:01,763 --> 00:15:07,285
[SPEAKER_00]: I know that the origins of it were not rooted in unwholesome roots, and that's all you can do, and that's all you need to do.

158
00:15:08,285 --> 00:15:14,768
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, any vipāka that comes, it's not mine, and it doesn't pertain to me, and it cannot make the mind turn against itself.

159
00:15:15,672 --> 00:15:24,836
[SPEAKER_00]: Because, again, you have ceased to provide that kind of unwholesome connection of lust, aversion, anger, distraction.

160
00:15:25,036 --> 00:15:28,937
[SPEAKER_00]: So, yeah, yeah, that's exactly what vipāka is.

161
00:15:29,137 --> 00:15:32,979
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't need to wait for future rebirths and so on to see the results of what you've been doing.

162
00:15:33,339 --> 00:15:34,860
[SPEAKER_00]: You are the result of what you've been doing.

163
00:15:35,380 --> 00:15:37,221
[SPEAKER_00]: Your habits are the results of what you've been doing.

164
00:15:39,041 --> 00:15:44,384
[SPEAKER_00]: And each time you choose to engage with results of what you've been doing, that's your new action, at that given time.

165
00:15:45,456 --> 00:15:46,557
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's not determinism.

166
00:15:46,577 --> 00:15:48,038
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not that you can't stop it.

167
00:15:48,279 --> 00:15:56,326
[SPEAKER_00]: Every single time you choose to accept those results of your actions as valid as whatever else and act out of them, that's your current choice.

168
00:15:57,007 --> 00:15:58,488
[SPEAKER_00]: That then perpetuates those results.

169
00:15:59,929 --> 00:16:00,550
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, exactly.

170
00:16:00,570 --> 00:16:06,696
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, that was... you know, at that even time of that kind of little story I was telling is...

171
00:16:08,800 --> 00:16:21,432
[SPEAKER_01]: I really kind of realized, okay, you know, this is the point, you know, this is why now the thing is not to try to get rid of these thoughts or try to kind of do something else on account of them, run away from them.

172
00:16:21,993 --> 00:16:27,518
[SPEAKER_01]: The point is to not feed this same thing that has given me now this pain.

173
00:16:28,218 --> 00:16:29,580
[SPEAKER_01]: And then immediately you know

174
00:16:30,370 --> 00:16:34,692
[SPEAKER_00]: And then the mind will say, yeah, but what if this pain lasts, you know, for a long time?

175
00:16:34,732 --> 00:16:35,192
[SPEAKER_00]: Doesn't matter.

176
00:16:35,773 --> 00:16:37,213
[SPEAKER_00]: What if it lasts for a year?

177
00:16:37,273 --> 00:16:37,794
[SPEAKER_00]: Doesn't matter.

178
00:16:37,874 --> 00:16:41,896
[SPEAKER_00]: What if for the rest of my life I don't get a moment of peace on account of this?

179
00:16:42,056 --> 00:16:42,316
[SPEAKER_00]: Fine.

180
00:16:43,256 --> 00:16:44,797
[SPEAKER_00]: Still, I won't act out of it.

181
00:16:45,578 --> 00:16:47,178
[SPEAKER_00]: Because the mind will say that.

182
00:16:47,218 --> 00:16:53,441
[SPEAKER_00]: The mind will make any of such endurances, it will make, like, it will throw the threat of infinity at you.

183
00:16:53,842 --> 00:16:55,983
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, this will forever now haunt you.

184
00:16:56,463 --> 00:16:58,184
[SPEAKER_00]: Because, see, you can't change what you did.

185
00:16:59,166 --> 00:16:59,987
[SPEAKER_00]: What you're going to do now?

186
00:17:00,347 --> 00:17:00,647
[SPEAKER_00]: Nothing.

187
00:17:00,947 --> 00:17:04,089
[SPEAKER_00]: I'll endure it for as long as it takes, even if it takes lifetimes.

188
00:17:04,309 --> 00:17:04,910
[SPEAKER_00]: But you won't.

189
00:17:05,610 --> 00:17:09,672
[SPEAKER_00]: It's an irrational sort of scare tactic, so to speak.

190
00:17:09,833 --> 00:17:15,556
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's, again, that's what Mahārāja was doing in the suttas, often with kind of trying to present you the worst case scenario.

191
00:17:16,176 --> 00:17:18,598
[SPEAKER_00]: But see, you have to accept it.

192
00:17:19,912 --> 00:17:23,254
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not like, okay, yeah, Mahārāja presents me the worst-case scenario, but it won't be.

193
00:17:23,354 --> 00:17:23,934
[SPEAKER_00]: It might be.

194
00:17:24,194 --> 00:17:26,095
[SPEAKER_00]: He might be right, and it might be forever.

195
00:17:26,295 --> 00:17:27,615
[SPEAKER_00]: It might be for the rest of your life.

196
00:17:28,076 --> 00:17:29,436
[SPEAKER_00]: That feeling will never change.

197
00:17:29,476 --> 00:17:31,137
[SPEAKER_00]: You're just going to be in perpetual pain.

198
00:17:31,657 --> 00:17:32,078
[SPEAKER_00]: Doesn't matter.

199
00:17:32,558 --> 00:17:34,359
[SPEAKER_00]: Still, you're going to endure it on the same level.

200
00:17:36,199 --> 00:17:44,943
[SPEAKER_00]: Because only by willing to endure it forever, so to speak, on that level, you would get to actually see where the problem really is.

201
00:17:45,183 --> 00:17:46,604
[SPEAKER_00]: And it's not in what you've done.

202
00:17:46,844 --> 00:17:48,685
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not in how long things will last.

203
00:17:49,325 --> 00:17:50,806
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not in what's happening to you.

204
00:17:51,006 --> 00:17:55,210
[SPEAKER_00]: It's in your present attitude of present craving against that discomfort.

205
00:17:55,831 --> 00:17:56,992
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's where the pain is.

206
00:17:57,612 --> 00:17:58,553
[SPEAKER_00]: That's where the problem is.

207
00:17:58,693 --> 00:18:08,642
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's why things... these things that you seemingly have to endure forever would... would haunt you and be painful only because you're resisting them here and now.

208
00:18:11,304 --> 00:18:12,064
[SPEAKER_01]: But you can.

209
00:18:12,945 --> 00:18:14,867
[SPEAKER_01]: Or at least, for me, it was...

210
00:18:15,484 --> 00:18:25,733
[SPEAKER_01]: It's very important to realize, like, I can endure it now, because I know that that's what I have to do, like, in that sense, and there's no confusion in that.

211
00:18:25,813 --> 00:18:26,334
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly, yeah.

212
00:18:26,514 --> 00:18:34,020
[SPEAKER_00]: And, you know, it doesn't matter how much pressure it kind of brings on to you, you know, but this is what needs to be done.

213
00:18:34,240 --> 00:18:38,965
[SPEAKER_00]: And that in itself, it's quite liberating, just the knowledge of what needs to be done correctly on the right level.

214
00:18:39,994 --> 00:18:46,056
[SPEAKER_00]: Because while that does not provide a sense of relief to people, it's because they don't see what needs to be done.

215
00:18:46,436 --> 00:18:47,816
[SPEAKER_00]: They assume what needs to be done.

216
00:18:48,256 --> 00:18:53,078
[SPEAKER_00]: They act out of sense of duty, what needs to be done and how needs to be dealt with.

217
00:18:53,458 --> 00:18:56,579
[SPEAKER_00]: But they don't really know and see for themselves what needs to be done.

218
00:18:56,699 --> 00:18:59,100
[SPEAKER_00]: And in this case, nothing, in a sense.

219
00:18:59,500 --> 00:19:00,880
[SPEAKER_00]: Nothing directly needs to be done.

220
00:19:01,380 --> 00:19:05,902
[SPEAKER_00]: You just need to endure on account of things you've already done or you already did.

221
00:19:07,731 --> 00:19:12,976
[SPEAKER_00]: And it's the same whether it comes to sensuality, aversion, any of the hindrances, basically.

222
00:19:13,737 --> 00:19:17,481
[SPEAKER_00]: When they try to pressure you and these thoughts revolve around you, that's how you deal with them.

223
00:19:18,181 --> 00:19:30,574
[SPEAKER_00]: That's how you go outside of their domain, by not, you know, jumping in and trying to address them and prevent them, manage them, justify them, explain them, rationalize them, psychologize them, and so on.

224
00:19:31,584 --> 00:19:35,967
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, and it is, I mean, the same principle for any of the hindrances, like the pressure of...

225
00:19:36,287 --> 00:19:37,007
[SPEAKER_00]: Doubt.

226
00:19:37,087 --> 00:19:41,510
[SPEAKER_01]: Doubt, sensuality, any of them, on account of how much you've been feeding.

227
00:19:41,530 --> 00:19:43,951
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the pain will be there, of that pressure.

228
00:19:44,711 --> 00:19:54,017
[SPEAKER_00]: How much you suffer on account of that pain, basically means, will be determined on how much you don't know what you need to do, what you need to do rightly, and how much you're resisting it.

229
00:19:55,077 --> 00:19:56,258
[SPEAKER_00]: That's how much you're going to suffer.

230
00:19:56,378 --> 00:20:01,821
[SPEAKER_00]: In and of itself, it does not necessarily mean suffering, even with all the discomfort that might bring on to you.

231
00:20:02,822 --> 00:20:04,763
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that would be the true end of karma.

232
00:20:05,784 --> 00:20:13,769
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's why it is like the whole surmounting of the hindrances, establishing the mind in the jhāna, it's basically surpassing.

233
00:20:14,977 --> 00:20:35,304
[SPEAKER_00]: The domain of action in vipāka, in that sense, it will, you know, now that depends on every individual, for how long you have to do it, but if you are doing it rightly, it will have to result in complete removal of the slightest traces of ownership, in regard to past, future, present, doesn't matter.

234
00:20:35,704 --> 00:20:39,706
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why Buddha said, the one who understands this, he doesn't even think anymore, I am.

235
00:20:40,801 --> 00:20:43,763
[SPEAKER_00]: I will be, and I was in the past, when he remembers.

236
00:20:43,863 --> 00:20:49,148
[SPEAKER_00]: That part of... Not that he forgot what he did in the past, or that the memories of the past are gone.

237
00:20:49,168 --> 00:20:59,155
[SPEAKER_00]: But the sense of ownership was always maintained in the present, through that ignorance, through that lack of knowledge, through that lack of clarity, through that constant ignorant engaging with those actions.

238
00:20:59,456 --> 00:21:05,000
[SPEAKER_00]: So now, he has approved to that, which means when he thinks of the past, he's not taking it up as mine.

239
00:21:06,067 --> 00:21:10,363
[SPEAKER_00]: When he has thoughts of future and what's gonna happen, what he's gonna do, he's not taking that up.

240
00:21:10,423 --> 00:21:10,885
[SPEAKER_01]: That's mine.

241
00:21:11,818 --> 00:21:22,107
[SPEAKER_00]: But, more often than not, that's too subtle for people to discern, so they just tend to default onto dismissing the past and the future, and mystifying the presence.

242
00:21:22,788 --> 00:21:24,449
[SPEAKER_00]: I heard it countless numbers of times.

243
00:21:24,550 --> 00:21:29,234
[SPEAKER_00]: Our past is no more, future is not yet, it's only the now, and stuff like that.

244
00:21:29,434 --> 00:21:37,581
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't even need the Buddha to tell you, but you still have your memories, even if you are perpetually dismissing the past, or refraining from thinking about the future.

245
00:21:38,342 --> 00:21:39,563
[SPEAKER_00]: See, that's the future idea.

246
00:21:40,003 --> 00:21:44,925
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, I shall sustain this idea in the future, where I will not think about the future, and thus I'll be free from the future.

247
00:21:45,605 --> 00:21:47,246
[SPEAKER_00]: But that's a contradiction in terms, again.

248
00:21:48,787 --> 00:21:56,410
[SPEAKER_00]: So, whether it's the present, whether it's... whether it's the past, whether it's the future, they are equally present, as past and as future.

249
00:21:57,550 --> 00:21:59,231
[SPEAKER_00]: So, and that's why... that's where the problem is.

250
00:21:59,931 --> 00:22:01,932
[SPEAKER_00]: Here and now, are you taking it up as mine?

251
00:22:02,593 --> 00:22:03,413
[SPEAKER_00]: Are you resisting it?

252
00:22:03,533 --> 00:22:04,353
[SPEAKER_00]: Are you dismissing it?

253
00:22:04,573 --> 00:22:05,294
[SPEAKER_00]: Are you afraid of it?

254
00:22:05,494 --> 00:22:07,895
[SPEAKER_00]: Are you affected by any hindrance on account of it?

255
00:22:08,960 --> 00:22:10,661
[SPEAKER_00]: And if the answer is yes, yeah, there you go.

256
00:22:10,681 --> 00:22:11,682
[SPEAKER_00]: Endure it on that level.

257
00:22:12,162 --> 00:22:16,186
[SPEAKER_00]: Don't concern yourself with, like, rewriting the past or preventing the future.

258
00:22:16,866 --> 00:22:23,071
[SPEAKER_00]: Just keep... keep an eye, keep a watchful eye on the doorway of your actions here and now.

259
00:22:24,292 --> 00:22:26,954
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, I don't know what I'm gonna do, but I know what I will not do.

260
00:22:28,695 --> 00:22:36,121
[SPEAKER_01]: So that way you know even... you don't have to worry about what specific thing I might do in the future, as long as I...

261
00:22:37,045 --> 00:22:38,806
[SPEAKER_01]: Know what I have to keep.

262
00:22:38,826 --> 00:22:41,106
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, because it doesn't matter what specific thing is done.

263
00:22:41,506 --> 00:22:43,747
[SPEAKER_00]: What matters is whether it was rooted in greed, aversion, delusion.

264
00:22:44,267 --> 00:22:48,428
[SPEAKER_00]: Sure, if there is no greed, aversion, delusion, certain specific things cannot be done.

265
00:22:48,928 --> 00:22:54,890
[SPEAKER_00]: But that's not because you are concerned about the specifics, but because you pulled out the roots that they would need to grow from.

266
00:22:54,910 --> 00:22:56,791
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that would be the true end of karma.

267
00:22:57,871 --> 00:23:00,091
[SPEAKER_01]: I think that's something probably quite hard for...

268
00:23:00,632 --> 00:23:03,913
[SPEAKER_01]: It's quite hard to understand, because... Well, it's like...

269
00:23:03,933 --> 00:23:05,393
[SPEAKER_01]: I think it was Nanaviera said it once,

270
00:23:06,986 --> 00:23:11,349
[SPEAKER_01]: Intention does not imply craving, which is a very hard thing to understand.

271
00:23:11,369 --> 00:23:15,572
[SPEAKER_00]: There is no craving without intention, but there is intention without craving.

272
00:23:16,252 --> 00:23:20,575
[SPEAKER_00]: But if you get to see that, you will be on the way of freeing yourself from craving, yeah.

273
00:23:22,056 --> 00:23:24,078
[SPEAKER_01]: Because as a... when you start

274
00:23:25,194 --> 00:23:27,895
[SPEAKER_01]: Intention equals, like, intention is craving.

275
00:23:28,675 --> 00:23:32,996
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's something, that's what you need to take that full blanket responsibility for it.

276
00:23:33,817 --> 00:23:37,198
[SPEAKER_00]: I am the owner of my actions, my choices, my intentions.

277
00:23:38,378 --> 00:23:44,900
[SPEAKER_00]: Even if, you know, I didn't act out of them, okay, so, but have I accepted them mentally?

278
00:23:45,440 --> 00:23:46,560
[SPEAKER_00]: Am I delighting in them?

279
00:23:46,620 --> 00:23:47,521
[SPEAKER_00]: Am I resisting them?

280
00:23:47,641 --> 00:23:51,162
[SPEAKER_00]: At least on that mental level, to that extent, you are involved.

281
00:23:52,424 --> 00:23:56,526
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's that whole, like, the, you know, learning how to endure things correctly.

282
00:23:57,366 --> 00:24:08,412
[SPEAKER_00]: Enduring on mental level, like, you had all these thoughts presenting themselves, trying to trap you, pull you, engage you, get you to lose perspective, basically, and try to deal with them specifically.

283
00:24:09,152 --> 00:24:09,733
[SPEAKER_00]: But you didn't.

284
00:24:10,113 --> 00:24:13,835
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you had to endure mind on the level of the mind, doing that.

285
00:24:14,455 --> 00:24:18,577
[SPEAKER_00]: There's nothing else you would have... you could have done by body or by speech that would have addressed it on that level.

286
00:24:19,903 --> 00:24:24,786
[SPEAKER_01]: Except try to distract yourself, but that only has a limited success, and sooner or later it will have to run out.

287
00:24:26,106 --> 00:24:29,268
[SPEAKER_00]: So, and that's, that's again, that's exactly what the practice is.

288
00:24:30,229 --> 00:24:41,054
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's what people can spend decades of practicing on the external level, but if they never allow things and take responsibility for them on that mental level, on the level of mental intention, there is no practice.

289
00:24:42,095 --> 00:24:43,816
[SPEAKER_00]: That is just the emulation of practice.

290
00:24:44,176 --> 00:24:47,638
[SPEAKER_00]: But internally, there are no, there's no proper basis established.

291
00:24:49,310 --> 00:25:03,439
[SPEAKER_01]: And if you're... and if you're not doing it like that, that's when, I think, it is so common, or at least, yeah, I was thinking like this previously as well, like, okay, I'll just keep going and, you know, keep trying.

292
00:25:03,479 --> 00:25:06,601
[SPEAKER_01]: At some point, the results of the practice will come.

293
00:25:07,361 --> 00:25:16,307
[SPEAKER_01]: And again, you can only really think like that if you're not fully taking responsibility for the fact that, wait, I'm not free from suffering right now, and everything that I'm doing is

294
00:25:16,974 --> 00:25:20,298
[SPEAKER_01]: Might be kind of perpetuating that, or... Yeah, yeah.

295
00:25:21,159 --> 00:25:35,776
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then, the kind of... because that's too unpleasant, the practice, the things you do, are kept on that external level, at the arm's length, which then also results in you expecting the results of your practice to come from that external level.

296
00:25:36,745 --> 00:25:38,606
[SPEAKER_00]: So, I have all this mess in my mind.

297
00:25:38,666 --> 00:25:40,247
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, I can't think about it or endure it.

298
00:25:40,267 --> 00:25:44,629
[SPEAKER_00]: Just, you know, be here now and Buddha and present is here and future is not yet and so on.

299
00:25:45,189 --> 00:25:49,551
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, I'll just do these motions and techniques and whatever else I commit myself to.

300
00:25:50,152 --> 00:25:54,694
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, hopefully, you know, I'm gonna have the experience arising as a result of it.

301
00:25:55,314 --> 00:26:00,097
[SPEAKER_00]: And all these bad things in my mind will be addressed and I will not be able to suffer anymore.

302
00:26:00,157 --> 00:26:02,198
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's the pure bliss and pure enlightenment.

303
00:26:04,189 --> 00:26:11,956
[SPEAKER_00]: And, yeah, I'm sure there were teachers in the Buddhist time, they would have advocated and advertised that, but the Buddha was quite clear that that's not where the practice is.

304
00:26:12,836 --> 00:26:19,882
[SPEAKER_00]: It's on the level of intention, wholesome, unwholesome, and, yeah, not losing perspective in regard to it.

305
00:26:20,703 --> 00:26:32,033
[SPEAKER_00]: Enduring it on that level, and that's that what he called the true tapas, the true kind of ascetic practice of, you know, you can endure the heat, the cold, the pain, the torture.

306
00:26:32,914 --> 00:26:43,624
[SPEAKER_00]: Endure things on that level of the thought and intention, without welcoming, delighting, or resisting, or trying to get rid, or justify, or psychologize, you are actually purifying your mind, whether you want it or not.

307
00:26:44,144 --> 00:26:45,945
[SPEAKER_00]: Because nobody wants to do it on that level.

308
00:26:46,625 --> 00:26:49,466
[SPEAKER_00]: And, at the same time, feel responsible for it.

309
00:26:49,507 --> 00:26:51,828
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, which is even worse, or harder.

310
00:26:53,068 --> 00:27:03,033
[SPEAKER_01]: And that... and the hard thing too, is like the... whether... when it's about the unwholesome and wholesome intentions, only you can really know

311
00:27:04,144 --> 00:27:05,045
[SPEAKER_00]: Where it was wicked.

312
00:27:05,085 --> 00:27:06,565
[SPEAKER_01]: When it's wholesome and unwholesome.

313
00:27:06,585 --> 00:27:06,746
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

314
00:27:06,766 --> 00:27:12,689
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's another reason that it's quite hard to feel fully responsible for it.

315
00:27:12,729 --> 00:27:15,511
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you can't ask somebody else necessarily for it.

316
00:27:15,551 --> 00:27:16,712
[SPEAKER_01]: Was it good or was it bad?

317
00:27:16,972 --> 00:27:18,773
[SPEAKER_01]: When you can, to an extent, but... Yeah.

318
00:27:18,793 --> 00:27:19,453
[SPEAKER_01]: ...in the beginning.

319
00:27:19,473 --> 00:27:22,355
[SPEAKER_01]: But really, ultimately, you have to know for yourself and...

320
00:27:22,375 --> 00:27:22,535
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

321
00:27:23,516 --> 00:27:25,917
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you need to start, like, doing your own digging.

322
00:27:26,898 --> 00:27:29,779
[SPEAKER_00]: Because that's not gonna just magically reveal itself.

323
00:27:29,839 --> 00:27:32,061
[SPEAKER_00]: Because the entire existence is about covering it up.

324
00:27:33,193 --> 00:27:46,640
[SPEAKER_00]: The sensuality, acting out of your will, distraction, all of that has in common the attitude of covering that very thing up, because it's unpleasant to recognize that it's on you, and you chose one thing, you could have chosen another.

325
00:27:46,660 --> 00:27:48,221
[SPEAKER_00]: Either way, it's on you.

326
00:27:48,841 --> 00:27:50,482
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you are fully responsible.

327
00:27:51,023 --> 00:27:53,484
[SPEAKER_00]: Whether you want to interpret that as everything is my fault,

328
00:27:54,840 --> 00:27:59,483
[SPEAKER_00]: Or in any other way, either way, responsibility is fully on you.

329
00:28:00,504 --> 00:28:07,289
[SPEAKER_00]: And even say, if you say for the sake of argument sake, if you're like practicing, yeah, everything is my fault.

330
00:28:08,750 --> 00:28:09,791
[SPEAKER_00]: What's the problem with that thought?

331
00:28:10,011 --> 00:28:11,132
[SPEAKER_00]: Why are you resisting that thought?

332
00:28:11,172 --> 00:28:12,213
[SPEAKER_00]: Why are you afraid of that thought?

333
00:28:13,882 --> 00:28:15,282
[SPEAKER_00]: Are you panicking when you think that?

334
00:28:15,722 --> 00:28:16,623
[SPEAKER_00]: Are you being overwhelmed?

335
00:28:16,683 --> 00:28:17,903
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay, that's your work.

336
00:28:18,063 --> 00:28:18,683
[SPEAKER_00]: Cut out for you.

337
00:28:19,283 --> 00:28:21,424
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you need to be able to even accept that thought.

338
00:28:21,584 --> 00:28:23,884
[SPEAKER_00]: Because the point will come when Māra will say that.

339
00:28:24,324 --> 00:28:26,005
[SPEAKER_00]: Everything is your fault.

340
00:28:26,045 --> 00:28:26,625
[SPEAKER_00]: Look what you did.

341
00:28:27,925 --> 00:28:31,606
[SPEAKER_00]: And there was numerous suttas in Therataryātara when he did exactly that.

342
00:28:31,906 --> 00:28:32,146
[SPEAKER_00]: See?

343
00:28:32,586 --> 00:28:33,567
[SPEAKER_00]: It's because of what you did.

344
00:28:34,287 --> 00:28:35,227
[SPEAKER_00]: Or what you wanted to do.

345
00:28:35,427 --> 00:28:38,788
[SPEAKER_00]: But then, you know, if monks and nuns had wisdom, they could see.

346
00:28:38,808 --> 00:28:40,348
[SPEAKER_00]: It's like, who are you talking about?

347
00:28:40,988 --> 00:28:42,949
[SPEAKER_00]: All there is is dukkha coming and dukkha going.

348
00:28:44,135 --> 00:28:51,461
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm not the owner of any of this because I've purified myself from that gratuitous ownership that has been maintained and perpetuated through greed, aversion, delusion.

349
00:28:51,962 --> 00:28:56,426
[SPEAKER_00]: So, yeah, now I just have to endure dukkha coming and going until it completely disappears.

350
00:28:57,907 --> 00:29:06,515
[SPEAKER_00]: But it's not going to be like a magical, kind of, a finger snap clearance, instantaneously freed from all of that.

351
00:29:06,535 --> 00:29:06,855
[SPEAKER_00]: No, no.

352
00:29:07,616 --> 00:29:11,539
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you're scared of certain thoughts, that's a problem.

353
00:29:13,623 --> 00:29:18,424
[SPEAKER_00]: You being overwhelmed by fear is a problem.

354
00:29:20,404 --> 00:29:25,745
[SPEAKER_00]: If it's impossible for you to remain unmoved by certain other thoughts, like sensuality, that's a problem.

355
00:29:26,525 --> 00:29:36,567
[SPEAKER_00]: If it's impossible, you know, for you to not have, then, thoughts of cruelty, hate, anger, when you're annoyed or irritated or offended or insulted, that's a problem.

356
00:29:37,467 --> 00:29:41,048
[SPEAKER_00]: So all those things that, again, are on the level of the mind,

357
00:29:42,337 --> 00:29:52,022
[SPEAKER_00]: If they move you, if they... if that passion sort of engages you and you cannot withstand it, you cannot endure it, you cannot but give in to it, that's a problem.

358
00:29:53,202 --> 00:29:55,783
[SPEAKER_00]: So that's why, like, you shouldn't kind of... well, I mustn't be thinking that.

359
00:29:55,823 --> 00:29:57,964
[SPEAKER_00]: No, you should be able to think whatever you want to think.

360
00:29:58,765 --> 00:30:02,707
[SPEAKER_00]: And the mind should not be able to overwhelm you on account of that.

361
00:30:03,573 --> 00:30:06,996
[SPEAKER_00]: So, yes, that doesn't mean you just in one go you think everything at once.

362
00:30:07,737 --> 00:30:14,683
[SPEAKER_00]: But, as I said, if such a thought of, as it came up in this example, also that means everything is my fault, comes up, well, maybe.

363
00:30:16,345 --> 00:30:17,125
[SPEAKER_00]: Am I afraid of that?

364
00:30:17,145 --> 00:30:19,087
[SPEAKER_00]: It doesn't matter if the answer is right or wrong.

365
00:30:19,147 --> 00:30:23,791
[SPEAKER_00]: What matters is, am I already trembling under the prospect, what if it is my fault?

366
00:30:24,051 --> 00:30:24,792
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, what if it is?

367
00:30:24,932 --> 00:30:25,413
[SPEAKER_00]: Maybe it is.

368
00:30:25,613 --> 00:30:27,114
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, in a way it is.

369
00:30:27,154 --> 00:30:27,815
[SPEAKER_00]: Let's say like that.

370
00:30:28,764 --> 00:30:32,166
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the worst-case scenario, whatever it is, is that moving you?

371
00:30:32,426 --> 00:30:33,187
[SPEAKER_00]: Is that frightening you?

372
00:30:33,387 --> 00:30:35,968
[SPEAKER_00]: If it is, to that extent, you are holding back.

373
00:30:36,409 --> 00:30:43,193
[SPEAKER_00]: To that extent, you are expecting shelter to come from the world, to prevent these thoughts and circumstances from arising, and that's not going to happen.

374
00:30:43,493 --> 00:30:45,014
[SPEAKER_00]: Or it's going to happen only for a period of time.

375
00:30:45,054 --> 00:30:49,777
[SPEAKER_00]: Sooner or later, it will have to change, and you will be fully exposed without a shelter, without safety.

376
00:30:52,198 --> 00:30:57,702
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, because, like, when you say, yeah, if you're not... if you're able to be moved by

377
00:30:59,013 --> 00:31:07,336
[SPEAKER_01]: Any of these kind of thoughts, it's a problem, but it's... it's my problem, as in it's my... it's my fault, even that.

378
00:31:07,616 --> 00:31:08,256
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, exactly.

379
00:31:08,276 --> 00:31:09,356
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the fault, see.

380
00:31:09,696 --> 00:31:12,297
[SPEAKER_00]: Not like, oh, you know, what I've done ignorantly and stuff.

381
00:31:12,737 --> 00:31:14,298
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, true, that's a relative fault.

382
00:31:15,738 --> 00:31:19,442
[SPEAKER_00]: Every time you acted out of greed or anger and so on, yeah, it's a relative fault.

383
00:31:19,802 --> 00:31:25,609
[SPEAKER_00]: What is the acute, here-and-now fault, is you being moved by that and accepting that.

384
00:31:26,009 --> 00:31:28,612
[SPEAKER_00]: And trying to outrun it, trying to get rid of it and so on.

385
00:31:28,752 --> 00:31:31,075
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the actual living fault.

386
00:31:33,854 --> 00:31:35,236
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's also not... Blemish.

387
00:31:35,656 --> 00:31:40,661
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, and it would be then easy to kind of think, okay, so I should not be moved by this.

388
00:31:41,162 --> 00:31:48,309
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, I should try, but you can't... you have to just stop again, like... Well, again, so you can think that, I should not be moved by this.

389
00:31:48,369 --> 00:31:51,172
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay, so where was this decision rooted in now?

390
00:31:52,254 --> 00:32:00,483
[SPEAKER_00]: In the fact that I was moved by it, and the fact that it was unpleasant, and the fact that I don't want that discomfort, thus, I will now decide to never be moved by it.

391
00:32:01,064 --> 00:32:07,010
[SPEAKER_00]: So, fundamentally, you're not really deciding to never be moved by it, you're just deciding to try to outrun the suffering, yet again.

392
00:32:07,691 --> 00:32:12,876
[SPEAKER_00]: But, see, you're gonna be doing that, every now and then, but if you do know where to look,

393
00:32:13,537 --> 00:32:30,002
[SPEAKER_00]: Such as, you know, the reasons for your actions, whatever those actions and decisions are, you will get to see, okay, yeah, I have had the thought of, I shall not be moved by this, but at the same time, I do still have perspective that not being moved means not acting out, including with the thought of, I shall not be moved by this.

394
00:32:30,282 --> 00:32:31,402
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's how you cease to be moved.

395
00:32:32,302 --> 00:32:33,563
[SPEAKER_00]: So then, that was the right thought.

396
00:32:33,863 --> 00:32:34,883
[SPEAKER_00]: It matched your experience.

397
00:32:34,943 --> 00:32:37,064
[SPEAKER_00]: I shall not be moved, and I haven't been moved.

398
00:32:37,584 --> 00:32:41,665
[SPEAKER_00]: At will, I can be now unmoved, because the craving has been removed.

399
00:32:42,488 --> 00:32:55,062
[SPEAKER_00]: Needless to say, of course, one will be able to see this correctly after the proper and thorough development of the gradual training that we so often described in many other videos.

